37097>>>>>    Function IsLoggedIn Returns Boolean
37099>>>>>        String sLoginName
37099>>>>>        Boolean bLogWebSession bLoggedIn
37099>>>>>        
37099>>>>>        Get pbLogWebSession to bLogWebSession
37100>>>>>        If not bLogWebSession Begin
37102>>>>>            Forward Get IsLoggedIn to bLoggedIn
37104>>>>>            Function_Return bLoggedIn
37105>>>>>        End
37105>>>>>>
37105>>>>>        
37105>>>>>        Get psLoginName to sLoginName
37106>>>>>        
37106>>>>>        Function_Return (sLoginName <> "")
37107>>>>>    End_Function
37108>>>>>    
37108>>>>>    
37108>>>>>    //
37108>>>>>    // This procedure is called when validating a session and after logging in. Its purpose is to 
37108>>>>>    // update properties based on the session and user data. Augment this function to update 
37108>>>>>    // properties based on the session / user table. Note that WebAppUser and WebAppSession contain
37108>>>>>    // the right records when this procedure is called.
37108>>>>>    //
37108>>>>>    // Params:
37108>>>>>    //      bClear   True if the procedure is called before session validation to clear properties.
37108>>>>>    //
37108>>>>>    Procedure UpdateSessionProperties Boolean bClear
37110>>>>>        Handle hoUserDD
37110>>>>>        
37110>>>>>        Get phoUserDD to hoUserDD
37111>>>>>        
37111>>>>>        //  Update user properties
37111>>>>>        If (not(bClear) and HasRecord(hoUserDD)) Begin
37113>>>>>            Set psUsername to (Trim(WebAppUser.FullName))
37114>>>>>            Set psLoginName to (Trim(WebAppUser.LoginName))
37115>>>>>            Set piUserRights to WebAppUser.Rights
37116>>>>>            
37116>>>>>            Send OnSessionPropertiesSet 
37117>>>>>        End
37117>>>>>>
37117>>>>>        Else Begin
37118>>>>>            Set psUsername to ""
37119>>>>>            Set psLoginName to ""
37120>>>>>            Set piUserRights to 0
37121>>>>>            
37121>>>>>            Send OnSessionPropertiesClear
37122>>>>>        End
37122>>>>>>
37122>>>>>    End_Procedure
37123>>>>>    
37123>>>>>    Procedure OnSessionPropertiesSet
37125>>>>>        //  Empty event stub
37125>>>>>    End_Procedure
37126>>>>>    
37126>>>>>    Procedure OnSessionPropertiesClear
37128>>>>>        //  Empty event stub
37128>>>>>    End_Procedure
37129>>>>>    
37129>>>>>    Procedure EndSession
37131>>>>>        Integer iErr
37131>>>>>        Boolean bLogWebSession
37131>>>>>        Handle hoSessionDD       
37131>>>>>        
37131>>>>>        Get phoSessionDD to hoSessionDD
37132>>>>>        Get pbLogWebSession to bLogWebSession
37133>>>>>        If not bLogWebSession Begin
37135>>>>>            Forward Send EndSession
37137>>>>>            Procedure_Return
37138>>>>>        End
37138>>>>>>
37138>>>>>            
37138>>>>>        //  Check if session exists
37138>>>>>        Send Clear of hoSessionDD
37139>>>>>        Get psSessionKey to WebAppSession.SessionKey
37140>>>>>        
37140>>>>>        Send Find of hoSessionDD EQ Index.1
37141>>>>>        If (Found) Begin
37143>>>>>            Set Field_Changed_Value of hoSessionDD Field WebAppSession.Active to "N"
37144>>>>>            Get Request_Validate of hoSessionDD to iErr
37145>>>>>            If (iErr) Begin
37147>>>>>                // this should not happen. If it does its a programming error
37147>>>>>                Error DFERR_PROGRAM C_$WebAppSessionValidateFailed
37148>>>>>>
37148>>>>>                Procedure_Return
37149>>>>>            End
37149>>>>>>
37149>>>>>            Send Request_Save of hoSessionDD
37150>>>>>        End
37150>>>>>>
37150>>>>>    End_Procedure
37151>>>>>
37151>>>>>End_Class
37152>>>>>
37152>>>
37152>>>Object oSessionManager is a cWebSessionManagerStandard
37154>>>End_Object
